The next morning, the whole team stands together in the office.
We are having our daily meeting.
I know this routine well.
Katrin has led the team for three years.
She asks us for our updates.
"Good morning, what did you all do yesterday?", Katrin asks.
Jonas talks briefly about his work.
Then Katrin looks at me.
"Maya, how is it going with you?", she asks.
"Jonas and I got a lot done yesterday," I say.
"I programmed the function."
"We also corrected a few errors together."
Katrin nods, satisfied.
"And what are you doing today?", she asks.
"I am continuing to work on the code," I explain.
"Then I will speak with our tester Sven."
Katrin notes the progress on her laptop.
"Super, that sounds good," she says.
She looks at her notes and moves on to the next colleague.
